## method_on_the_wrong_type (exit 1)
error[Z0401]: `n_rows` cannot be called on an Int
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:1
  |
1 | 5.n_rows()
  | ^ this is an Int
  |
  = help: `n_rows` takes a Frame first; `x.n_rows(...)` is `n_rows(x, ...)`

## method_of_core_on_text (exit 1)
error[Z0401]: `abs` cannot be called on a Str
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:1
  |
1 | "a".abs()
  | ^^^ this is a Str
  |
  = help: `abs` takes a Float first; `x.abs(...)` is `abs(x, ...)`

## signature_differs (exit 1)
error[Z0205]: `sqrt` has the signature `Fn(Int) -> Float`, but `Fn(Int) -> Int` is needed here
 --> scripts/main.zeff:7:7
  |
7 | apply(sqrt, 4)
  |       ^^^^ `Fn(Int) -> Float`
  |
  = help: a function passed as a value matches the parameter types and the return type exactly, defaults ignored; write a function with that signature

## signature_differs_script_function (exit 1)
error[Z0205]: `double` has the signature `Fn(Int) -> Int`, but `Fn(Float) -> Float` is needed here
 --> scripts/main.zeff:7:8
  |
7 | applyf(double, 3)
  |        ^^^^^^ `Fn(Int) -> Int`
  |
  = help: a function passed as a value matches the parameter types and the return type exactly, defaults ignored; write a function with that signature

## not_a_function (exit 1)
error[Z0401]: `f` of `apply` must be a Fn(Int) -> Int, but this is an Int
 --> scripts/main.zeff:7:7
  |
7 | apply(5, 1)
  |       ^ an Int
  |
  = help: usage: `apply(f: Fn(Int) -> Int, x: Int)`

## no_such_function (exit 1)
error[Z0103]: no function is called `nope`
 --> scripts/main.zeff:7:7
  |
7 | apply(nope, 1)
  |       ^^^^ not a function
  |
  = help: a parameter of type `Fn(Int) -> Int` takes the bare name of a function with that signature

## too_many_through_value (exit 1)
error[Z0407]: `f` takes 1 argument, but more were given
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:41
  |
2 | fn two(f: Fn(Int) -> Int) -> Int { f(1, 2) }
  |                                         ^ one too many
  |
  = help: `f` is a `Fn(Int) -> Int`

## too_few_through_value (exit 1)
error[Z0406]: `f` needs 1 argument, but 0 were given
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:37
  |
2 | fn none(f: Fn(Int) -> Int) -> Int { f() }
  |                                     ^ `f` is a `Fn(Int) -> Int`
  |
  = help: give every argument the function type names

## named_through_value (exit 1)
error[Z0404]: `f` is a function value and takes positional arguments only, not named
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:43
  |
2 | fn named(f: Fn(Int) -> Int) -> Int { f(1, x: 2) }
  |                                           ^ not positional
  |
  = help: a function type names its parameters' types, not their names, so arguments are given in order

## wrong_type_through_value (exit 1)
error[Z0401]: argument 1 of `f` must be an Int, but this is a Str
 --> scripts/main.zeff:2:39
  |
2 | fn text(f: Fn(Int) -> Int) -> Int { f("a") }
  |                                       ^^^ a Str
  |
  = help: `f` is a `Fn(Int) -> Int`

## function_name_alone (exit 1)
error[Z0101]: nothing is called `abs` here
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:9
  |
1 | let f = abs
  |         ^^^ not a binding
  |
  = help: `abs` is a function; call it with parentheses: `abs(...)`
